    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1097">

                <pb facs="0963" n="859" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg859"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/9660.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to
                            Japan to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-11-11T13:00:00+09:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Nov. 11, 1913—1 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s November 7, 10 p.m.</p>
                <p>[The Minister for Foreign Affairs being absent, the Department’s telegram was
                    communicated through the Vice-Minister for Foreign Affairs. The rest of this
                    telegram relates to information that Japan is supplying Mexico with arms.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Guthrie</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
